{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>An oracle.</b> This pericope is attached, because he mentioned 'a sword upon his arm'; he mentioned when this will be and where it will be. And now he explains that this will be when Israel returns with Messiah son of Joseph to Jerusalem. And now this prophecy concerns Israel. The reason for mentioning now 'who stretches out the heavens' and 'who founds the earth' is that but for Israel, they would not have been created. And the reason for 'and who forms the spirit of man within him' is that he is a microcosm corresponding to heaven and earth. And this matter requires a lengthy exposition."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads 'דבקה היא' (it is attached); rendered as 'is attached' in the sense of connected to the preceding pericope."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:51.152648860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}